== 7. Future Considerations ==

=== Scribunto/Lua Migration ===

For complex validation logic, consider migrating to Lua modules:

```lua
local p = {}

function p.validateInfobox(frame)
    local errors = {}

    if not frame.args.name or frame.args.name == "" then
        table.insert(errors, "Missing required parameter: name")
    end

    local score = tonumber(frame.args.confidence_score)
    if not score or score < 0 or score > 1 then
        table.insert(errors, "confidence_score must be between 0.0 and 1.0")
    end

    return errors
end

return p
```

=== Cargo Alternative ===

For strict type validation, consider Cargo extension:

```wiki
{{#cargo_store:_table=Concepts
|Name={{{name|}}}
|Definition={{{definition|}}}
|EpistemicStatus={{{epistemic_status|}}}
|ConfidenceScore={{{confidence_score|}}}
}}
```

Cargo provides:
* Schema-level type validation
* NOT NULL constraints
* Enum value restrictions
* SQL-like querying

